WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.520
Here we are using an invisible table to
align the labels and entry fields, like

00:06.520 --> 00:11.960
this, date, colon, answer here, first
name, colon, answer here, and last name,

00:12.100 --> 00:17.640
colon, answer here. And you can see this
by going to the table design and actually

00:17.640 --> 00:24.400
showing the borders. So while this looks
neat visually, it creates a major problem

00:24.400 --> 00:29.500
for accessibility. For people who use
screen readers, the software doesn't see a

00:29.500 --> 00:35.500
simple form. Instead, it announces table
with two rows and four columns, then they

00:35.500 --> 00:40.700
have to navigate cell by cell, reading out
row one, column three, date, then row one,

00:40.840 --> 00:45.880
column four, answer here. A much better
and simpler approach is to remove the

00:45.880 --> 00:52.460
table entirely and just use line breaks.
So the form just ends up being date,

00:52.660 --> 01:00.420
colon, enter, first name, colon, enter,
and last name, colon, enter on separate

01:00.420 --> 01:06.520
lines, like this. And now I can delete the
form or

01:08.530 --> 01:14.630
delete the table, and we end up with a
simple, the simplest design.

